WEBVTT

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.640
We will soon be 
entering Japan's airspace.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.600
If we go any further, we will be 
in violation of their airspace.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.580
It will cause an
 international incident.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.940
Here is fine.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.500
It has been an honor to accompany a living 
legend like yourself, Silver Grizzly.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.700
I wish you 
luck in battle!

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.100
<i>Now then, should we 
head back home?</i>

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.980
<i>Yeah, let's hurry 
back and have a drink.</i>

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.960
The other worlds are Monolium, 
Disfia, Tetra-Heaven and Tritomy.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.460
Then we have Septpia, the 
world where we humans live.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.380
My head is killing me.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.720
I drank too much yesterday.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.800
And Septpia is the only world in which

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.640
we may open Gates that connect 
to various other worlds.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.890
Huh? Was there an emergency 
drill scheduled today?

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.280
No idea.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.150
I wonder what it could be?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.110
The air raid alarm? No way.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.890
Is it a Foreigner?

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.290
Okay, okay. 
Everyone calm down.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.400
Let's wait for further instructions.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.420
She's right!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.720
Something's flying towards us!

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:14.250
Huh? Where? I can't see a thing.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.820
Can you actually see it, Lion?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.510
Yup! It's over there.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.780
Come on, look.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.920
I can't see it.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.850
It's just a little speck.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.090
And it's getting bigger and bigger.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.890
I'm not getting any Foreigner signals.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.720
<i>We have identified a missile approaching.</i>

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.660
So you really did see it.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.570
Yup.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.410
Miss Kagura! Shouldn't you 
be evacuating the students?

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.790
Calm down.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.440
This academy is under ALCA's 
jurisdiction.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.820
There's no way it'll fall 
to conventional weaponry.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:53.920
The system is programmed to automatically 
destroy any approaching unknowns.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.130
Did we shoot it down?

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.120
What's with that!?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.320
All right, everyone! Move back!

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.990
Cover your ears and open your mouths.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.240
I'll shoot you down.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.230
She did it!

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.830
What?

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.090
You've got to be kidding!

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.880
What is that?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.150
Amazing.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.400
Lion!

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.110
No need to worry.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.170
The glass in these 
windows is reinforced.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.900
Even armor-piercing ammunition 
won't get through.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.570
And certainly not a simple—

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.580
Senpai!

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.160
What are you doing, Daddy?!

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:33.760
Daddy?

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.060
Lion!

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.620
Lion! I missed you so much!

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.250
I brought this bouquet of—

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.110
I'm sorry!

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.070
They're ruined, even though I went through 
the trouble to bring them from the garden.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.950
But I've got lots of other treats from home!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.780
Lion, what's going on?

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.230
Um…

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.670
So you're my daughter's homeroom teacher?

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.850
As expected, you're very skilled.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:57.860
And you are?

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.330
Sorry, I should have introduced myself.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:03.360
My name is Strafansky Yelistratova.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.480
I'm Lion's father.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.840
Lion, introduce your daddy to everyone!

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.930
Daddy, you idiot!

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.860
Why?!

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.600
Mr. Yelistratova, we would appreciate 
if you would contact us

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.030
beforehand should you 
wish to visit the school.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.100
I did contact you.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.990
And was it not you who 
refused me, Vice Principal?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:40.420
What I refused was your request to 
live in the dorms with your daughter.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.310
And what's the problem with that?!

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.920
Cut it out!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.090
You're causing trouble for 
everyone here at the school.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.920
That's what I hate about you!

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.340
H-a-t-e?!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.860
Lion! Why?!

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:55.540
Why don't you get it?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:59.500
I just want to be here with you!

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.310
This sure comes as a surprise.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.270
He makes Lion-san look normal.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.040
There really is no Foreigner response.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.530
But of course. He's obviously human.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.700
Even if a human and a Foreigner had that 
kind of relationship, they couldn't have kids.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:19.280
Aw. He was so strong, I thought he 
might be a new type of Foreigner.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.290
I've had enough of you!

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.760
What are you all doing here?

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.610
Huh? Even Nina-chan.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.970
Thanks for letting us watch.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:36.640
Lion.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.950
I just… I…

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.330
I came all the way from 
Liones just to see you!

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:44.400
I've had enough of you!

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:45.650
Just go home already!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.420
What's Liones?

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:54.570
Liones is the name of the country 
from which Lion hails from.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.770
You named your daughter 
after your country's name?

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.980
That kind of creeps me out.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.850
No, well…

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:07.770
I don't think anybody wants 
a father that's too clingy.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.360
If your father heard that, I think he'd cry.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.890
But I get it.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.090
See? Listen to what everyone's saying.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:18.350
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Lion.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.040
Teens can be so hard on their fathers.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.490
Including this current uproar,

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.760
this is turning into quite a problem.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.190
It sure is.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.990
We even fired off anti-aircraft weaponry.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.060
It's been a while since I've used 
a Stinger. It felt pretty good.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:38.280
While I can't say I condone the variety of
unconventional actions that took place today…

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.010
Yeah.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.620
I do understand how you 
feel, Mr. Yelistratova.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.780
Just for today, we will make a special exception

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.760
and allow you to sit in on 
your daughter's lectures.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.900
I'm so grateful! So grateful!

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.970
Spasibo! Spasibo!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:06.480
There is one Foreigner 10 km ahead of you
 and two Foreigners 30 km ahead of you. 

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.310
There are a number of students who think that 
math isn't a necessary skill for Logicalists.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.480
But a good battle strategy has 
its foundations in good math.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.230
Let's see.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:12.020
If you were 10 km away and 
moving at 300 km/hour, then…

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:13.590
Um…

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.490
Use your daddy's fingers!

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.260
If that's not enough, how about my toes too?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.660
Mr. Yelistratova, please 
be quiet during class.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.710
Oh, pardon me.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.430
Looks like I got in trouble!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.500
Lion!

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:33.800
Please don't leave me all alone!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.680
Don't follow me!

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.370
But you used to get lost in our own castle.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.720
What will you do if you get 
lost in a school this big?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.830
I'm going to the bathroom!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:53.240
Do your best, Lion!

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:59.010
Logicalists that have Tranced will 
 experience a sudden increase in their powers.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.530
But it's up to each Logicalist to decide 
how they want to use that power.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.220
If you rely on strength alone,

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.080
you'll never win the battle.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.460
While it's good to be skilled in 
battle, with a strong defense,

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:13.080
your chances of success will rise remarkably.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.090
I'm sure that's something 
you understand, Miss Kagura.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.560
I thought that you'd miss 
some of the food from home.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.110
So I asked your mother to 
make all of your favorites

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.850
and brought them with me.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:35.780
Does it taste good?

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.450
I'm sure it does!

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.350
I helped to make this one.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.650
He's so nice.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.340
What's the matter, Lion?

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:49.570
Keep on eating!

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:51.440
There's no reason to hold back.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.010
I don't want any more.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:56.460
Look, here's some ezhiki your mother 
made for you. You like those, don't you?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.220
N-Not really.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:01.970
Your mother would be sad 
if she heard you say that.

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.060
For now... I'm fine.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.810
So you're not hungry?

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:12.650
Then have this rose.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.340
The scent will make you relax,

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.190
and your appetite will be back in no time.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.890
I took off the thorns, so 
there's no need to worry.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.280
Just leave me alone already!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.430
Lion?

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.080
Start your Trance!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.460
Gate Access! Tritomy!

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.550
Let's do this, Selen.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.480
<i>Target identified. Executing mission.</i>

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:08.740
Amor.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.000
<i>Right.</i>

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:11.940
Qipao.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.250
<i>Okay, okay.</i>

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:16.670
Rosa.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:17.750
<i>Yes.</i>

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:25.200
Even if this is a mock battle, keep 
in mind that you've actually Tranced.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.890
Make sure to stay focused.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.280
Got it.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:33.590
Nina-san! I hope you don't 
mind practicing with me!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.520
Sure.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.110
Let's go!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:48.030
Lion! Do your best! Don't lose!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.780
Lion! Watch your footwork.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:53.290
Remember the roadwork we'd 
do together every morning!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.360
Step, step!

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:57.330
We used to sing while running, remember?

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:00.340
Come on! Step, step!

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.100
Why me too?!

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.760
I cannot bear such a disgrace.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:13.980
I suppose I shall have to quickly end this.

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:18.940
I won't let you win so easily!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.990
What are you doing! Stop this instant!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.000
How tasteless!

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.080
I'm gonna win with this!

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:47.780
What?!

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:48.880
This is just nuts.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.390
Mistress!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:53.970
Lion!

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:07.240
Why do you guys always, always, 
always cause trouble?!

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.030
We're sorry.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:12.900
But since we're already 
all the way over here,

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:15.660
we should just take it easy 
until they come for us.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:19.420
Come now, this isn't the time nor the
place to be acting so carefree.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.540
Right, Nina-san?

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:23.250
So fluffy.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.600
A bear cub!

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.500
Pretty cute.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.230
You know what?

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:31.120
I think it might be best to put some 
distance between us and the cub.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.220
Y-You're right.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:37.480
What would we do if its parent 
found us in the mountains out here?

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:45.890
Nina-chan, I think that cub 
might belong to that brown bear.

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:47.240
So fluffy.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:52.560
Um... I've heard that bears can be pretty 
ferocious when it comes to their babies.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.000
It's true.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:58.140
Daddy always told me to stay away 
from grizzlies with their children.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.430
I see.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.760
As we were saying! That brown bear's 
baby is that cub that you're holding!

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.450
Nina-san, let go of the cub! Let go!

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.130
So fluffy.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:13.390
This is a translation machine for 
the Language of Foreigners.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.860
This is a machine to blow on ramen.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.500
No, not the radar.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.320
Huh? A Foreigner response?

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.880
Who cares about that! Just run!

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:23.040
But a human could never outrun a bear.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:28.170
Here it is! A bear repellent machine 
that puts out a frequency that bears hate!

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.950
Switch on!

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:44.880
We were tracking them by 
detecting Belle's Paradox Level.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.370
But ten or twenty minutes ago,

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:50.120
it appears as though an avalanche struck 
the area we last traced that response to.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.300
Avalanche?

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.190
Please let us come.

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.500
I'mma come too!

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:57.310
No.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:59.300
Leave this to us.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.680
What about Lion-san's father?

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:03.020
He already left.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:05.800
Straight north.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:12.780
<i>You're right that Lion demonstrated high 
Logicalist powers from a young age.</i>

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:17.520
<i>I established this country to 
protect her from ALCA.</i>

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:22.790
<i>I protected her by stopping her
from being conscripted.</i>

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:26.030
<i>I have no intention of 
handing her over to you now.</i>

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.920
<i>We do understand how you feel.</i>

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:34.020
<i>She's like a metronome without a tempo.</i>

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.930
<i>But that means if she doesn't 
know how to use her power,</i>

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.560
<i>she will one day cause a huge catastrophe.</i>

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:42.480
<i>That's...</i>

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.060
<i>Please trust us.</i>

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.440
<i>For your daughter's sake as well.</i>

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:04.190
L-Lion.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:13.340
We've fallen into a pretty deep pit.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.580
All things considered, 
things aren't looking good.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:18.300
Nina-chan, you have a really high fever.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:20.920
I'm so cold myself that I feel 
like I'll catch a cold, too.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:23.720
At any rate, we have to 
do something or else—

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.110
I know now's not the time, 
but I'm really hungry.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.160
How could you be thinking about that when—

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.820
Lion!

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.460
Those roses!

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:53.250
I'm sure that Daddy will find these.

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:55.490
Good idea, Lion.

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:58.510
We have to get Nina-san to a hospital soon.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.990
What is it? This isn't the time—

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.460
The brown bear!

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:06.140
Again?!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.990
We don't have anywhere to run!

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.150
We're nothing but skin and 
bones! Not at all tasty!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.400
Daddy.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.150
Sorry for keeping you waiting, Lion.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:19.320
Daddy!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.370
For Lion!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:44.940
So you too...

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:47.680
You're just like me, aren't you?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.360
Daddy!

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.460
Nina-chan.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.800
Where am I?

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.380
In your room.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.870
And everyone's safe and sound,
 so you can relax.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:21.730
Mistress, we were so worried!

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:25.810
No going off on your own again, okay?

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.420
You guys.

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.180
Sorry for making you worry.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.690
Isn't it great that we're all okay?

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:35.210
I am responsible for this entire event.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:36.940
I am very sorry.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:39.990
No, it's not your fault.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:43.950
It's my fault for being 
embarrassed about you.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:47.900
I realized that you're just
 worried about me.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:51.940
There's an angel standing in front of me!

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:55.540
Lion, I'm so happy that 
you understand how I feel!

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.020
But...

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:59.800
you don't need to worry about me anymore.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.650
I've got lots of friends now!

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:07.310
Every day is full of fun 
because I have them with me.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:12.580
Right. Every time you 
grow, it makes me happy!

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:16.060
I guess kids really can grow up
without their fathers!

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.560
Are you hungry?

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:23.920
I still have the homemade food your mother 
made that you didn't eat for lunch.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:25.340
Want it now?

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:26.250
Yeah!

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:31.340
All right! Let's go back to the dorm and eat.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:33.710
I'm looking forward to seeing your room.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.570
Thanks, Daddy. See you later!

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.670
Why are you acting so cold?

00:20:38.980 --> 00:20:40.010
Our dorm is—

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:43.420
Men can't come into an all-girl dorm.

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.010
Let's eat it all together.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.230
What a treat!

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:49.870
I would be overjoyed to share in 
sampling the foods of your homeland.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.000
Let's go, Karin, Karen.

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:56.870
N-No!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.980
Dasvidania!

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.980
Episode 3

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.980
The Silver Grizzly
—There is No Love Like a Child's—

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:34.480
I can't take this without a drink!

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:36.320
What am I supposed to do?

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:38.440
Please! Somebody tell me!

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:43.000
All dads like this do is build up aggro
from their daughters.

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:46.340
I'd be happy to teach you.

00:22:46.630 --> 00:22:50.800
Mr. Yelistratova, are you familiar 
with the phrase "give and take"?

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.410
Give and take. And what do you desire?

00:22:55.590 --> 00:22:58.550
Perhaps an opportunity to 
network with some single guys?

00:22:58.550 --> 00:23:03.800
So basically, you're saying you want a 
Japanese style social, an event much like a mixer.

00:23:03.800 --> 00:23:06.310
A mixer?! Do you really 
understand what she wants?

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:18.500
Next Episode

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:07.490
Leave it to me!

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:09.750
I'm acquainted with 
celebrities the world over.

00:23:09.750 --> 00:23:11.980
Celebrities? Amazing!

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:13.280
Mr. Yelistratova, what 
time's good for you?

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:15.300
I'm good for the
 beginning of the month!

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:16.370
Let's get everything
 set up right.

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:18.500
Hey, Mr. Yelistratova, what 
kind of hot guys do you know?

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:21.580
Let's see. The Wolf of Siberia.

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:22.900
The Lightning Bolt of Kremlin.

00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:26.450
Oh, and the Giant of Tiefu
 has 
 divorced and is now single!

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:29.300
Aren't those members of the 
army, and not celebrities?

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:30.520
I'm all for it!

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:32.770
Aren't guys that are 
stronger than you the best?

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:34.100
Totally!

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.730
Then let's have some
 more to drink!

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:38.720
Give me some of 
that sweet potato liquor!

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.060
So you're down with that?
